  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "ration-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 620,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "PRESS ROOM - riso study desk.\n\nThe daily ration strip in every header is the spine of this design: 20 ticks, filled as you spend, so the invisible budget becomes a physical object you can read at a glance."
    },
    {
      "id": "money-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1260,
      "w": 560,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "The two buttons carry different weight on purpose. Preview is a dashed, weightless outline. Generate is a knockout block that prints its own cost on the face: 'spends 4 of your 20'."
    },
    {
      "id": "deadair-note",
      "x": 1560,
      "y": 2380,
      "w": 560,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Generating names the wait instead of hiding it - 'waiting 24s for the rate limit... this pause is the limiter, not a stall'. Dead air only reads as broken when nothing explains it."
    },
    {
      "id": "dark-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 640,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "Same design, one token set swapped - nothing moves. The spot blue lightens so it still reads as the action colour, and the difficulty ramp lifts so all three stay separable on a dark card. Measured ratios are on the Foundations page."
    },
    {
      "id": "quota-dark-note",
      "x": 1560,
      "y": 2240,
      "w": 560,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "The ration block inverts rather than dimming: in dark mode it becomes a light slab on the dark ground, so 'you are out' still lands as the heaviest thing on the page."
    },
    {
      "id": "alt-note",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": 680,
      "w": 700,
      "page": "page-3",
      "text": "Two alternates, low-fi on purpose. Each names its own trade-off so this is a real choice and not a rigged vote. Say the word and either becomes the main direction."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "page-2"
  }
}